STATEMENT: >>>
Four nodes the sheet could not file under a topic.

- The line between flake checks and devenv tasks is undrawn; five grammar checks are written twice; neither system is a joint. See [LINK: MECH-CHECK-SYSTEM-BOUNDARY]. Speaks about [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-MECHANISM]. [UNADDRESSED]
- Two known problems — vocabularies copied three times over in Python, and milestone two's rules sitting in the tool (a judgement still pending) — have no owner and no work node. See [LINK: MECH-MILESTONE-TWO-SEMANTICS-MISPLACED] and [LINK: MECH-SDOC-VOCABULARY-SINGLE-SOURCE]. Speaks about [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-MECHANISM]. Feeds [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-SEMANTICS-LIVE-IN-TOOLS-WITH-NO-OWNER]. [GAP]
- The mechanism that was to draw the boundary between defining semantics and this system's own semantics is dissolved — the layer stack draws it. The edge from code to its layer is still unplaced. See [LINK: DEC-LAYER-STACK] and [LINK: MECH-SEMANTICS-DEFINITION-BOUNDARY]. Speaks about [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-MECHANISM]. Feeds [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-SEMANTICS-LIVE-IN-TOOLS-WITH-NO-OWNER]. [FALLS OUT: DEC-LAYER-STACK draws it; code -> layer edge unplaced]
- The executable-rules probe has run and is the evidence behind the roadmap decision. Its retirement condition is unmet. See [LINK: DEC-EXECUTABLE-RULES-ROADMAP] and [LINK: SPIKE-EXECUTABLE-RULES]. Speaks about [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-EVIDENCE] and [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-DECISION]. [WORKS]
